rts of the theorem are true too. Therefore, according to the theorem, only option III gives us a true statement:  \n\n*If the system $[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]x=0$ has the unique zero solution, then, $det[\\begin{aligned}a & b \\\\ c & d\\end{aligned}]\\ne 0$ .* $\\,✓$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065987/state.json" "file_sha256" "4713558b4f351438f7b24d355d9b9bb43b537f322660cc6b17328e79c53de0f3"} {"question" "q-128151" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065987/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "f7d3087baf55591da19e797c183909e7f6b4eb60e0a79522f295cd288037478e"} {"question" "q-128151" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065987/state.json" "file_sha256" "4713558b4f351438f7b24d355d9b9bb43b537f322660cc6b17328e79c53de0f3"} {"question" "q-128151" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "I and II only"] ["text" "I and III only"] ["text" "I only"] ["text" "II only"] ["text" "III only"]] "category" "ma_complete_choices" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065987/state.json" "file_sha256" "4713558b4f351438f7b24d355d9b9bb43b537f322660cc6b17328e79c53de0f3"} {"question" "q-128151" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/text "III only"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14065987/state.json" "file_sha256" "4713558b4f351438f7b24d355d9b9bb43b537f322660cc6b17328e79c53de0f3"}] "usage" {"q-47653" [] "